       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <div class="blog-content">
               <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SSC Delhi Police Answer Key 2025-26 Released" class="blog-hero-image">
               <div class="blog-body">
                 <h1 class="blog-title">SSC Delhi Police Constable Answer Key 2025-26 Released: Objection Window Now Open – Direct Link Here!</h1>

                 <p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) has brought a crucial update for all candidates who appeared in the Delhi Police Constable (Executive) Examination 2025. The much-awaited provisional answer key for both Male and Female candidates has been officially released on January 13, 2026! Along with the answer key, the commission has also activated the objection window, allowing candidates to challenge any discrepancies they find. This is a critical period for all aspirants to review their performance and take necessary action.</p>

                 <p>The Computer-Based Examination (CBE) for 7565 Constable vacancies was successfully conducted from December 18, 2025, to January 6, 2026, across various centers. Now, candidates can access their individual response sheets and the provisional answer key on the official SSC website, ssc.gov.in. This release allows you to estimate your scores and prepare for the next stages of the recruitment process.</p>

                 <div class="highlight-text">
                   <strong>Important Dates to Remember:</strong> The objection window is open only for a limited period, from January 13, 2026, to January 16, 2026 (until 6:00 PM). Make sure to submit your challenges before the deadline to avoid any last-minute issues.
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">How to Download Your SSC Delhi Police Answer Key 2025-26</h2>
                 <p>Accessing your answer key and response sheet is a straightforward process. Follow these steps carefully:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official SSC Website</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the Staff Selection Commission's official website: <a href="https://ssc.gov.in" target="_blank">ssc.gov.in</a>.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Answer Key Section</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, click on the "Answer Key" tab.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">3. Find the Relevant Link</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Look for the notification titled "Constable (Executive) Male and Female in Delhi Police Examination-2025: Uploading of Tentative Answer Keys along with Question Paper(s) cum Response Sheet(s)" and click on it.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">4. Log In</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a login page. Enter your Registration Number/Roll Number and Password/Date of Birth as per your admission certificate.</div>
                 </div>
                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">5. Download Your Response Sheet and Answer Key</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">After successful login, your individual response sheet and the provisional answer key will be displayed. Download and save the PDF file for future reference and score calculation.</div>
                 </div>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Raising Objections Against the Answer Key</h2>
                 <p>If you believe there is an incorrect answer in the provisional key, you have the opportunity to challenge it. Here’s what you need to know:</p>
                 <div class="benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ <strong>Objection Window:</strong> January 13, 2026, to January 16, 2026 (6:00 PM).</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Fee per Objection:</strong> A processing fee of ₹50/- is charged for each question challenged. This fee is generally non-refundable unless the objection is accepted.</p>
                   <p>✅ <strong>Submission Mode:</strong> Objections must be submitted online through the SSC portal. Representations received after the deadline or through any other mode will not be entertained.</p>
                 </div>
                 <p>It is crucial to submit valid proof along with your objection. After the objection window closes, the SSC will review all received challenges. A final answer key will then be released, and the results of the Computer-Based Test will be prepared based on this final key.</p>

                 <h2 class="section-title">Calculating Your Estimated Score</h2>
                 <p>Once you have your response sheet and the answer key, you can calculate your tentative score. While specific negative marking details should be confirmed from the official notification, generally, 0.25 marks are deducted for each incorrect answer.</p>
                 <p><strong>Formula for Estimated Marks:</strong></p>
                 <p class="highlight-text">
                   (Number of Correct Answers × 1) - (Number of Incorrect Answers × 0.25)
                 </p>

                 <h2 class="section-title">What Happens Next? (Expected Result Date)</h2>
                 <p>Following the closure of the objection window and the review process, the SSC will announce the final answer key and subsequently, the Delhi Police Constable Result 2025-26. Based on previous trends, results are typically released approximately 30-45 days after the objection window closes. This means you can expect the results sometime between late February and early March 2026.</p>
                 <p>Candidates who qualify in the Computer-Based Test will proceed to the next stage of the selection process, which includes the Physical Endurance Test (PET) and Physical Standard Test (PST) conducted by the Delhi Police.</p>

                 <div class="benefit-card">
                   <p>✅ Download your Answer Key and Response Sheet immediately.</p>
                   <p>✅ Carefully review all answers against the provisional key.</p>
                   <p>✅ If you have strong evidence, raise objections before January 16, 2026 (6 PM).</p>
                   <p>✅ Keep an eye on the official SSC website for further updates on the final answer key and results.</p>
                 </div>

                 <p>We wish all candidates the best of luck with their results and future endeavors!</p>
               </div>
             </div>
       </div>
    
            
